      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "A chef bought $80$ ounces of spices and paid $$45.60$ for them. What's the unit price per pound?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert from ounces to pounds. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we divide the number of ounces by $16:$     \n\n$$\n80÷16=5\n$$\n\nSo, $80$ ounces is the same as $5$ pounds. Now, to find the unit price per pound, we divide the total price by $5:$ \n\n$$\n45.60÷5=9.12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the spices cost $$9.12$ per pound.",
